abstract: >
  Garuda is a modern distributed programming language inspired by Erlang/OTP,
  written 100% by an Indonesian developer. It features actor model concurrency,
  pattern matching, destructuring, list/map comprehension, pipeline operator,
  native HTTP server, and VM-based runtime (GVM). Garuda is designed for
  building web servers, microservices, and distributed systems with
  Indonesian-flavored syntax.

